READING: the lemma holds iff (a) per-ratio errors track maxCF (the Diophantine
dichotomy), (b) the generic instance's speed-ratios have small maxCF and small
errors, (c) the near-dilation's ratios have LARGE maxCF (small rationals a/b:
w = a * b^{-1} has huge CF spike) and carry the big errors -- the exception set
arithmetically = the S225 quarantined family, and (d) the variance sits at the
ACZ scale. Then t2 is CLASSICAL: linear completion + CF dichotomy per-ratio +
ACZ on average; no Weil required.
